{
  "high_level_description": "A delicate botanical line-art border of live oak branches with Spanish moss framing the top edge of a wide horizontal panel, drawn in single-weight forest green ink on a warm cream background.",
  "compositional_deconstruction": {
    "background": "Warm cream background filling the entire panel, completely unadorned in the lower two-thirds. Quiet, restrained vintage herbarium sensibility with no shading, fills, gradients, or color beyond the forest green line work above.",
    "elements": [
      {
        "type": "obj",
        "desc": "Live oak branch running horizontally across the top edge of the panel in single-weight forest green ink. Gnarled twisting trunk segment on the left transitions into finer secondary branches reaching rightward. Dense canopy of small live oak leaves clustered along the upper branch, each leaf a closed oval outline with a single central vein. Long wispy strands of Spanish moss hang in soft curving drapes from the lower side, varying lengths, some trailing down to roughly one-third into the panel, rendered as delicate parallel hairline strokes suggesting fibrous texture. Smaller secondary oak sprigs branch downward at the left and right ends with scattered leaves and shorter moss tendrils. Heaviest mass centered, symmetrical balance between ends."
      }
    ]
  }
}

{
